// expect: refuse E_ResumeOutsideArm
// A resume stands where a continuation exists: an arm, or a lambda or nested
// fn minted inside one, whose record holds the arm's k. `drive` is a
// top-level fn an arm calls, so it holds none, and its resume is refused
// where it stands. Until 2026-10-16 the class reported and the program
// compiled anyway, the k handed to `drive` as a hidden trailing argument;
// the nested form is mn-resume-in-called-fn.mn.
effect Choice {
  pick() -> Int
}

fn drive() = resume(1) + 1

handler twice {
  pick() => drive(),
}

fn main() = pick() + 3 ~> twice
